{"title":"1957 AHSME Problems/Problem 24","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If the square of a number of two digits is decreased by the square of the number formed by reversing the digits, \nthen the result is not always divisible by: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/f/e6f3698f1a883a4b5c022b5ab1d07da3cd8785d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 9 \\qquad  \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\text{the product of the digits}\\qquad  \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\text{the sum of the digits}\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\text{the difference of the digits}\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"849\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the first number have digits <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/a/b5a7034b881dd7f82661bd23f5fc7d0beac976f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\underline a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/f/fafb3c463ddd05a2bc51089b8a447aa048133f8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\underline b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"18\" />. Then, it equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/8/8c8b0d985d7137b67edcdd55029a03843223fe5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"14\" />, and the second number equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/6/91637b4521e1c07f0aa214e1070b7c2f81c10967.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10b+a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" />. Taking the difference of the squares of these two numbers and simplifying, we see that:\n</p><p>\\begin{align*}\n(10a+b)^2-(10b+a)^2 &amp;= ((10a+b)-(10b+a))((10a+b)+(10b+a)) \\\\\n&amp;= (9a-9b)(11a+11b) \\\\\n&amp;= 9 \\cdot 11(a-b)(a+b)\n\\end{align*}\nThus, the result in question is always divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/2/4f2aee761704bb62a779d1bbcb9fb09912bb516f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a-b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/e/1be092b2283c00c376e719c5f650a15433d43a28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" />. This fact eliminates all of our options except <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/a/81ab9f67d76fae7201391c3b46d8306c736ed30d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{\\textbf{(B) }the product of the digits}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"226\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px s